{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/007-continue.json\"","aggregated_output":"{\"command\":\"story-continue\",\"version\":1,\"status\":\"ok\",\"outcome\":\"ready-for-verification\",\"result\":{\"resultId\":\"23323e5d-5bb0-4577-b214-e0c38318b97f\",\"provider\":\"claude-code\",\"model\":\"claude-fable-5\",\"role\":\"story_implementor\",\"sessionId\":\"4de8d8b1-5d3a-4643-b6ad-a0c0a326f4fa\",\"continuation\":{\"provider\":\"claude-code\",\"sessionId\":\"4de8d8b1-5d3a-4643-b6ad-a0c0a326f4fa\",\"storyId\":\"03-message-projection-tokens\"},\"outcome\":\"ready-for-verification\",\"story\":{\"id\":\"03-message-projection-tokens\",\"title\":\"Story 3: Message Projection and Token Estimates\"},\"planSummary\":\"Fixed F-03-002. openThreadDatabase now performs an identity check before any migration runs: a read-only probe (so the probe itself cannot mutate an invalid file) requires schema version >= 1, a thread_metadata table, and the metadata singleton row that thread creation writes transactionally. Files failing the check — an empty database, an unrelated SQLite database, a non-database file — are rejected as caller_error/thread_not_found ('exists but is not an lhc thread file') with no lhc tables created and user_version untouched; SQLite's 'not a database' refusal is classified as the same identity failure, while other open errors remain system_error. The opener's signature changed to OpResult<DatabaseSync> so the rejection flows through the standard result contract, and all three call sites (runMessageEvents, runListEvents, listMessages) propagate it. Valid Story 2 user_version=1 files pass the check (they carry the metadata row) and still migrate lazily to v2, so F-03-001 behavior is preserved — all prior migration tests stay green. Three focused tests prove rejection-without-mutation for an existing empty file (verifier's exact probe), an unrelated SQLite database with foreign data, and a plain text file.\",\"changedFiles\":[{\"path\":\"packages/lhc/src/domains/threads/internal/create.ts\",\"reason\":\"Added validateThreadFile (read-only identity probe: version >= 1, thread_metadata table, singleton row) run before migrations; openThreadDatabase now returns OpResult<DatabaseSync>, rejecting non-thread files as caller_error/thread_not_found and wrapping environment failures as system_error\"},{\"path\":\"packages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts\",\"reason\":\"runMessageEvents and runListEvents consume the opener's OpResult, returning the rejection instead of opening/migrating arbitrary files\"},{\"path\":\"packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/index.ts\",\"reason\":\"listMessages consumes the opener's OpResult, so read-back on a non-thread file fails instead of adopting the file\"},{\"path\":\"packages/lhc/test/thread-migration.test.ts\",\"reason\":\"Added an F-03-002 describe block: three rejection tests asserting error class/code and, below the SDK, unchanged user_version, no lhc tables created, foreign data and raw bytes intact; F-03-001 tests unchanged above it\"},{\"path\":\"packages/lhc/test/red-manifest.json\",\"reason\":\"Re-recorded thread-migration.test.ts hash after appending the F-03-002 tests\"}],\"tests\":{\"added\":[\"test/thread-migration.test.ts: listMessages against an existing empty database file fails with caller_error/thread_not_found, user_version stays 0, no tables created (the verifier's exact F-03-002 probe)\",\"test/thread-migration.test.ts: messageEvents against an unrelated SQLite database fails, creates no lhc tables, leaves user_version at 0 and the foreign rows intact\",\"test/thread-migration.test.ts: a non-SQLite text file is rejected as caller_error/thread_not_found by both listMessages and messageEvents with its bytes byte-identical afterward\"],\"modified\":[],\"removed\":[],\"totalAfterStory\":72,\"deltaFromPriorBaseline\":14},\"gatesRun\":[{\"command\":\"npx vitest run test/thread-migration.test.ts test/projection.test.ts\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"pnpm --dir packages/lhc run green-verify\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"pnpm --dir packages/lhc run verify-all\",\"result\":\"pass\"}],\"selfReview\":{\"passesRun\":0,\"findingsFixed\":[\"F-03-002: the lazy opener no longer creates lhc schema on, or returns successful read-back from, arbitrary existing files — a read-only identity probe (schema version >= 1 plus the thread_metadata singleton) gates migration, invalid existing files are rejected as caller_error/thread_not_found without any mutation, and Story 2 user_version=1 files still migrate lazily (all F-03-001 tests remain green)\"],\"findingsSurfaced\":[\"The 'not a database' classification relies on SQLite's error message text to distinguish identity failures from environment failures; node:sqlite exposes no stable error code for SQLITE_NOTADB, so a wording change in a future Node release would downgrade that case to system_error (still a rejection, never adoption) — worth a glance when bumping the Node engine\",\"thread_not_found is reused for 'exists but is not a thread file' because the epic's error-code set is closed; the reason string distinguishes the cases. If operators need to tell them apart programmatically, a dedicated code would be a vocabulary addition for a future story\",\"The read-only probe adds one extra open per SDK operation on a thread file; negligible at v1 scale, and it is the only way to guarantee the probe itself cannot mutate an invalid file\"]},\"openQuestions\":[],\"specDeviations\":[],\"recommendedNextStep\":\"Re-verify F-03-002 with the new rejection tests (the original empty-file probe now returns caller_error/thread_not_found with user_version still 0 and no tables); F-03-001 coverage is unchanged and green. Then proceed to Story 4, whose turn tables should land as a version-3 migration behind the same validated opener.\"},\"errors\":[],\"warnings\":[],\"artifacts\":[{\"kind\":\"result-envelope\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/007-continue.json\"}],\"startedAt\":\"2026-06-10T14:11:13.607Z\",\"finishedAt\":\"2026-06-10T14:16:02.012Z\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
